---
title: About
description: More about this website.
bodyClass: page page--about
---
<section class="page-section page-section--about">
    <div>
        <h1>About</h1>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
        <p class="lede">
            This project is a collection of aerial photographs taken
            around Lincolnshire, and captured
            by <a :href="profile.website" @text="profile.name" class="link" rel="me external"></a>
            using consumer drones.
        </p>

        <hr />

        <p>
            I first started flying drones in the summer of 2017, when I purchased
            a small entry-level consumer drone; the DJI Spark. In September 2025,
            I upgraded to the newly released DJI Mini 5 Pro.
        </p>

        <p>
            I love how these devices allow you to see and appreciate the world from
            not just great heights but a whole new perspective. I enjoy taking it to
            familiar places and seeing what new angles I can capture.
        </p>

        <hr />

        <h3>How this site is built…</h3>

        <p>
            The project is built using the static site generator
            <a href="https://www.11ty.dev" class="link" rel="external">11ty</a>.
            It uses WebC as the templating language.
            The design uses plain HTML, BEM-based CSS, and a small amount of
            JavaScript for progressive navigation behaviour.
        </p>

        <p>
            The cursor icons are from <a href="https://heroicons.com" class="link" rel="external">Heroicons.</a>
            The icons for Exposure Time, Aperture, Focal Length, Camera, and Flash
            are by Denis Klyuchnikov from
            <a href="https://thenounproject.com" class="link" rel="external">Noun Project</a>.
        </p>

        <p>
            A few packages are used to build specific features. The EXIF data is pulled using the
            <a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/exifr" class="link" rel="external">exifr</a> package,
            and <a href="https://lokeshdhakar.com/projects/color-thief/" class="link" rel="external">colorthief</a> is used
            for the photo colour palette. <a href="https://blurha.sh" class="link" rel="external">
            BlurHash</a> is used as photo placeholder during loading.
            The 360-degree photos use <a href="https://pannellum.org" class="link" rel="external">Pannellum</a>,
            a lightweight WebGL panorama viewer. The carousel gallery is powered by
            <a href="https://swiperjs.com" class="link" rel="external">Swiper</a>.
            Google Maps is used to show the locations.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div>
        <a href="/" class="button">Browse the Photos</a>
        <a webc:if="profile.website.length" :href="profile.website" rel="me external" class="button button--secondary">Visit my Website</a>
    </div>
</section>
